# Python build and tool artefacts. The repository root .gitignore has no Python
# entries (it predates this directory) and is owned by another stream, so the
# gate carries its own: running the suite creates __pycache__/, .pytest_cache/
# and .ruff_cache/ here, and none of them belongs in a commit.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Local virtualenvs. The development instructions in README.md create .venv.
.venv/
venv/

# Belt and braces. The gate holds no credential of any kind: it runs as its own
# service account and reads tokens from the metadata server (design doc §12.2).
# A key file appearing here would be a review failure, not a gitignore problem,
# but it must never be committed by accident either.
*-key.json
service-account*.json
